<title>USA: Muni bar at 'pay-to-play' ethics crossroads - Levitt.</title>
<headline>Muni bar at 'pay-to-play' ethics crossroads - Levitt.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Citing growing public cynicism of lawyers, SEC's chairman on Thursday urged attorneys nationwide to adopt a New York City bar proposal to end &quot;pay-to-play&quot; by municipal bond lawyers.</p>
<p>&quot;Shady practices in the municipal market today have placed lawyers at an ethical crossroads,&quot; Arthur Levitt told market participants meeting in Philadelphia, according to a written text of the Securities and Exchange Commission chief's address.</p>
</text>
